Dial every offered relay at once, and start without the ones that are not up in time.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, on top of 0002 (upstream PR #26).

Why: PR #26 binds every relay in the offer, one after the other, each with a 12 s
connect timeout. A relay that blackholes its handshake therefore held the whole call
for 12 s before any media flowed, once per such relay. Now every relay is dialled
concurrently, the fanout starts once the first is up and the others had 2 s to join,
and a relay that connects later is closed. Found in the review of
fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387.

